"""Assemble the report from frozen metrics and source reconciliation."""
from pathlib import Path
import json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
M=json.loads((R/'analysis/overlap_metrics.json').read_text())
S=M['semantic_alignment']
Q=json.loads((R/'analysis/source_reconciliation.json').read_text())
B=[]
def p(text): B.append({'kind':'paragraph','text':text})
def h(text,level=1): B.append({'kind':'heading','text':text,'level':level})

p('The overlap test supports the main distinctions used in the bounded Bitcoin Core reconstruction, while exposing continuing instability in institutional classification. All three fresh AI contexts agreed on candidate screening for all 24 sampled records. Among 58 one-to-one statement matches, all three agreed on all seven compared labels in 29 cases. Source reconciliation remains necessary because shared labels do not establish correctness and majority voting can miss supported interpretations.')
p('The practical implication is to retain the existing reconstruction, add the overlap evidence, clarify several coding conventions, and qualify the absolute translation-freeze claim. This round does not justify a claim that the entire institutional model or source corpus has been validated.')
h('Design and scope')
p('Three fresh AI contexts independently received the same 24 focal records from six linked 2025 contribution episodes: PRs 32359, 32381, 32406, 32714, 33224, and 33453. The study reused the complete Round 4 sample, comprising 12 purposive records, six deterministically sampled candidate records, and six deterministically sampled excluded records. These are known research materials, not a previously unseen holdout. The identical packet contained 98 entries, including surrounding exchanges, dated guidance, patches, and metadata.')
p('The study froze project specification 0.3, its schema and checker, the source bytes, selection, instructions, and comparison plan before dispatch. Each coder used a fresh context without the parent conversation, earlier annotations, other coders’ answers, or the earlier conclusions. The same inherited model configuration served all three runs; this was not a comparison of distinct model families. Provider snapshot, sampling parameters, token use, and costs were unavailable. The filesystem was shared and access restrictions were instructional rather than technically enforced; coder access records are self-reports.')
p('Each coder preserved a first complete annotation, ran the supplied checker, conducted one source-based self-review, and froze the final output. The first checks reported six mechanical issues for A and three for C; B passed its first check. All final annotations passed the coordinator’s repeated checker, covering 1,952 exact anchor references in total. These checks establish structural and quotation integrity, not semantic correctness. First and final versions, recorded changes, flags, and instructions remain in the evidence package.')
p('A separate fresh context aligned the focal statements with the seven comparison labels withheld. Component text remained visible to distinguish analytical layers, so masking was incomplete. Another fresh context reviewed all 24 focal sources, including agreements, against the codebook and relevant context; it did not receive the prior baseline or agreement scores. After the coding outputs froze, the coordinator reviewed the alignment and sources, reconciled findings, and assessed implications for the inherited analysis.')
h('Agreement before reconciliation')
p('All coders classified the same 22 focal records as containing candidates and the same two as context only. Their focal statement counts were 62, 71, and 70. Forty-one statements had identical spans across all three coders. Source-based alignment identified 58 one-to-one groups, one split/combined group, 13 groups with missing counterparts, and two unresolved groups. Every one of the 203 focal statement records appears exactly once in this mapping.')
labels={'grammar':'Grammar','deontic_force':'Deontic force','institution.type':'Institutional type','institution.standing':'Institutional standing','institution.dispute_present':'Dispute flag','statement_target_level':'Statement target level','observed_action_level':'Observed action level'}
rows=[]
for key,label in labels.items():
    v=S['fields'][key]; n=v['unanimous']; d=v['total']
    rows.append([label,f'{n} / {d}',f'{100*n/d:.1f}%'])
rows.append(['All seven labels together',f"{S['all_fields_unanimous']} / {S['one_to_one_triple_denominator']}",f"{100*S['all_fields_unanimous']/S['one_to_one_triple_denominator']:.1f}%"])
B.append({'kind':'table','caption':'Unanimous agreement across the three submitted final annotations','headers':['Compared field','Agreement','Percent'],'rows':rows,'widths':[4.1,1.5,1.3],'center_columns':[1,2],'note':'Denominator: 58 one-to-one statement groups. These descriptive rates precede reconciliation and are not accuracy estimates. They do not include component-role, relation, or outcome-claim agreement.'})
p('Institutional type showed the least agreement. Overall governance-level agreement was higher, but the difficult majority and transparency statements produced substantial differences. The high overall rate largely reflects routine operational statements and should not obscure uncertainty in rarer higher-level interpretations.')
p('The matched denominator covers 174 of the 203 statement records. The remaining 29 records belong to the split/combined group, missing-counterpart groups, or unresolved groups; they are retained rather than counted as agreements. The two unresolved groups concern how a quoted premise and a tentative 150-byte refinement attach to the focal units, even though the full annotations retain these details in context or evidence. Pairwise results and every group mapping are available in the package. Multiple statements from one source are not independent observations.')
h('Findings from source review')
for item in Q['report_findings']:
    h(item['title'],2);p(item['text'])
h('Implications for the existing analysis')
p('Twelve of the 46 inherited statement units used in Round 11 occur in the focal records. The shared context also permits comparison of the supplied repository-state sequence, but the present study does not independently retest all platform-event findings, podcast coding, the original Paper 1 sample, or the full comparative model. Within this scope, the source review does not require rebuilding the central reconstruction.')
p('The most concrete inherited annotation change concerns U32: explicitly record the challenge to the absolute translation-freeze claim’s application. Two other inherited units, U02 on review weighting and N16 on transparent decision-making, merit a clearer preferred grammatical representation. All three fresh coders used regulative parses; the earlier constitutive representations can preserve related meaning, so this is a matter for explicit harmonization rather than an automatic finding that the institutional conclusions were wrong.')
p('Retain the evidence distinctions already present in the earlier analysis: local recognition of the conditional warning principle, a general documented moderation procedure versus a particular announced sanction, and documented release responsibilities versus deference on one backport decision. The separate baseline-impact ledger identifies proposed changes and retained findings. It does not alter the inherited files or manuscript.')
h('What the working paper can claim')
p('The study now has an overlapping AI repeatability test on a defined sample, with preserved independent submissions, mechanical checks, explicit proposition alignment, and revisable source-based reconciliation. The results support presenting these stages as an integrated analytical method. They also identify where the method needs sharper conventions: recognition versus ordinary assent, the scope and date of documentary support, institutional type, analytical layers, and higher-level governance claims.')
p('The evidence does not establish cross-model robustness, population accuracy, a human reference standard, causal identification, or superior speed and cost. No numerical threshold defined a pass. The comparison measures consistency conditional on this sample, packet, specification, and workflow. Source reconciliation is another inspectable AI judgment, and defensible alternatives remain visible.')
h('Evidence package')
p('The evidence package contains the frozen protocol and sources, first and final annotations, comparisons, independent audit, reconciled findings, and baseline-impact ledger. Its README identifies the principal files and reproduction commands. Scripts verify integrity and recompute agreement; the source interpretations remain inspectable judgments.')
out={'title':'Overlapping AI validation of Bitcoin Core governance coding','subtitle':'Round 12  |  Research methods assessment  |  November 7 2026','blocks':B}
(R/'report/report_content.json').write_text(json.dumps(out,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Prepared',len(B),'report blocks.')
